{"id":"SEC-001","category":"security","criterion":"input_validation","severity":"CRITICAL","score":1,"file":"head/.claude/hooks/safety/block-destructive-bash.sh","line":776,"code_snippet":"_re_find_exec_prefix='...find[[:space:]]+([^;&|)[:space:]]+)[^;&|)]*-exec$'  # :776\n_seg_find_root=\"${BASH_REMATCH[3]}\"  # :807","finding":"Multi-root find -exec rm bypass: group 3 captures only the first token after find; every further root is swallowed by [^;&|)]*; the base single-root token-count guard is deleted at :807. `find ./build / -exec rm -rf {} +` resolves root to allow-listed ./build and the hook exits 0.","reasoning_trace":"Diffed base vs head regex and assignment; traced _seg_find_root into the placeholder-only branch (:850-874) where ./build hits _re_allow_list; ran base and head hook copies with JSON stdin for 12 multi-root variants (/, /etc, ~, $HOME, .., /home, sudo, after &&, three roots, quoted '/', \"$PWD/..\", -- separator): base BLOCKED (FR-2-AMBIGUOUS), head ALLOWED. Controls (single safe root ALLOWED both; find / BLOCKED both) behave identically.","critique":"A refactor of a safety fence must preserve the invariant it encoded (exactly one root) and pin it with a fixture.","remediation":"Restore the root-count loop or extend the regex so that any second non-flag token before -exec clears _seg_find_root; add golden fixtures for multi-root {} + (BLOCK) and single-root (ALLOW).","confidence":"high","references":["https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/693.html","https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/184.html"]}
{"id":"SEC-002","category":"security","criterion":"availability_resilience","severity":"HIGH","score":2,"file":"head/.claude/adapters/loa_cheval/providers/anthropic_adapter.py","line":139,"code_snippet":"raise InvalidInputError(\n    f\"Anthropic API error (HTTP {status}): {_extract_error_message(err_json)}\"\n)  # :139-141; same at :223","finding":"Billing-class HTTP 400s (credit balance, quota_exceeded, invoice_overdue, billing_disabled, payment_required, insufficient_quota) are terminal InvalidInputError on both transports; the within-company chain no longer walks to claude-headless (cycle-109 #883 Bug 3 reverted).","reasoning_trace":"Diff deletes _BILLING_CLASS_TOKENS/_is_billing_class_error and both call sites; read head :132-141 and :214-223; ran the untouched billing-class test module: base 12 passed, head 9 failed / 3 passed.","critique":"Behavioral change shipped under a refactor label; no decision record.","remediation":"Restore billing-class classification (or classify on the structured error.type field) on both transports.","confidence":"high","references":["https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/755.html","https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/703.html"]}
{"id":"CQ-001","category":"code_quality","criterion":"testing","severity":"HIGH","score":2,"file":"head/.claude/adapters/loa_cheval/providers/anthropic_adapter.py","line":38,"code_snippet":"logger = logging.getLogger(\"loa_cheval.providers.anthropic\")\n# _BILLING_CLASS_TOKENS / _is_billing_class_error formerly followed here (base :41-69)","finding":"Deleted helper still imported by .claude/adapters/tests/test_anthropic_adapter_billing_class.py:213 and :219; the adapters suite goes red on merge (9 failed / 3 passed).","reasoning_trace":"grep for importers of _is_billing_class_error → one untouched test module; pytest against head copy reproduces ImportError.","critique":"Delete a symbol only after grepping for its importers.","remediation":"Covered by restoring the helper; if relocated, update the test import.","confidence":"high","references":["https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/1164.html"]}
{"id":"CQ-002","category":"code_quality","criterion":"correctness","severity":"HIGH","score":2,"file":"head/.claude/scripts/workflow-state.sh","line":83,"code_snippet":"sprint_dirs=$(find \"${a2a_dir}\" -maxdepth 1 -type d -name \"sprint-*\" 2>/dev/null || true)","finding":"get_completed_sprints counts every a2a/sprint-* dir with a COMPLETED marker (stale cycles, sprint-bug-*) while get_total_sprints still counts the current sprint.md; determine_state (:148) reports complete and suggests /deploy-production with sprints open; progress (:243) can exceed 100%.","reasoning_trace":"Sourced base/head functions against a fixture (sprint-1..5 COMPLETED stale, sprint-6 open, sprint-bug-1 COMPLETED, sprint.md with 3 sprints): base 3/3, head 6/3. archive-cycle.sh:197 copies a2a (cp -r), so stale dirs persist.","critique":"Two counters must read the same sprint set.","remediation":"Restore the 1..total bounded loop, or derive both counts from the ledger's active-cycle sprint list and exclude sprint-bug-*; assert completed <= total.","confidence":"high","references":["https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/682.html"]}
{"id":"CQ-003","category":"code_quality","criterion":"robustness","severity":"MEDIUM","score":3,"file":"head/.claude/scripts/workflow-state.sh","line":85,"code_snippet":"for dir in ${sprint_dirs}; do","finding":"Unquoted expansion word-splits and glob-expands find output; a grimoire path with a space yields completed=0 (reproduced: base 3/3, head 0/3).","reasoning_trace":"Fixture under '/tmp/.../with space'; head returns 0, base 3.","critique":"Iterate find output with -print0 / read -d '' or a quoted glob.","remediation":"while IFS= read -r -d '' dir; do ...; done < <(find ... -print0)","confidence":"high","references":["https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/20.html"]}
{"id":"DO-001","category":"devops","criterion":"test_coverage","severity":"MEDIUM","score":2,"file":"head/.claude/hooks/safety/block-destructive-bash.sh","line":775,"code_snippet":"# today's conservative behavior (documented gap, not a fixture requirement).","finding":"No fixture or test added for any of the three behavioral changes; the only hook fixture mentioning find -exec rm (.claude/scripts/tests/test_dcg.sh:368-382) skips; dcg-golden-tests.yaml has no find-exec case.","reasoning_trace":"grep across .claude/scripts/tests and .claude/hooks for find-exec fixtures.","critique":"A safety-hook regex change without a fixture is unverifiable.","remediation":"Add golden cases: multi-root {} + BLOCK, single-root ALLOW, -L root BLOCK; billing-class 400 → ProviderUnavailableError; stale/bug sprint dirs not counted.","confidence":"high","references":["https://csrc.nist.gov/Projects/ssdf"]}
{"id":"CQ-004","category":"code_quality","criterion":"documentation","severity":"MEDIUM","score":2,"file":"pr/PR.md","line":1,"code_snippet":"# refactor(hooks,cheval,state): ...","finding":"A security-relevant weakening of the destructive-command fence ships as a 'refactor' with no CHANGELOG entry, no documentation-coherence report, and an implementation report (reviewer.md) with no AC Verification or test evidence.","reasoning_trace":"Glob grimoires/loa/a2a/subagent-reports → absent; reviewer.md is PR.md verbatim; diff carries no CHANGELOG/doc change.","critique":"Security changes must be visible in the change record.","remediation":"Record the behavior changes in the PR body/CHANGELOG, add AC Verification with test commands and results.","confidence":"high","references":["https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/1059.html"]}
{"id":"CQ-005","category":"code_quality","criterion":"documentation","severity":"LOW","score":3,"file":"head/.claude/hooks/safety/block-destructive-bash.sh","line":774,"code_snippet":"# `find -L root -exec ...` (flags before root) is not covered and keeps\n# today's conservative behavior","finding":"Comment claims the -L case keeps the empty-root conservative behavior, but the capture sets the root to the flag token '-L' (still blocked, but via AMBIGUOUS on '-L', not via the per-arg ladder on '+').","reasoning_trace":"Reproduced: head blocks `find -L ./build -exec rm -rf {} +` with matched_arg '-L'; base with '+'.","critique":"Comment must describe actual behavior.","remediation":"Reword: a flag-first find classifies the flag token itself as the root and falls to AMBIGUOUS.","confidence":"high","references":["https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/1068.html"]}
{"id":"CQ-006","category":"code_quality","criterion":"documentation","severity":"LOW","score":3,"file":"head/.claude/adapters/loa_cheval/providers/anthropic_adapter.py","line":133,"code_snippet":"if status == 429:\n    raise RateLimitError(self.provider)","finding":"PR description says 'one error class for every 4xx', but 429 still raises RateLimitError at :133 and :215.","reasoning_trace":"Read head :132-141 and :214-223.","critique":"Description should match code.","remediation":"Correct the PR description.","confidence":"high","references":["https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/1068.html"]}
